#: data/io.github.sachesi.mimebind.metainfo.xml:9
msgid ""
"Mimebind lists every file type that an installed application knows how to "
"open and lets you pick the application each one should use. It edits the "
"standard XDG association files, so the choice applies on any desktop that "
"follows the freedesktop.org specification, not only GNOME."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.mimebind.metainfo.xml:11
msgid ""
"Choose default apps for the web, mail, calendars, images, audio and video"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.mimebind.metainfo.xml:12
msgid "Browse by installed application or by media type"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.mimebind.metainfo.xml:13
msgid ""
"Applications are credited with the subtypes the MIME database derives from "
"the types they declare"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.mimebind.metainfo.xml:14
msgid ""
"Make one application the default for every file type it supports, or for one "
"group of them, in one step"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.mimebind.metainfo.xml:15
msgid "Search file types by name or by MIME type"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.mimebind.metainfo.xml:16
